WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:03.160
- Okay, so I had kind of a
crazy afternoon the other day.

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:06.719
My producing partner, Amber,
25 years we've been together.

00:00:06.719 --> 00:00:08.141
She's right over there.

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:08.974
(audience clapping)

00:00:08.974 --> 00:00:09.807
Go Amber!

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:12.580
So we helped out a dog,

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:15.160
that had been involved in a hit and run.

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:16.930
And what happened was, okay,

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:18.870
so our friend Prika starts
crying and screaming

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:20.260
and we're like, what's going on?

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:23.730
And so he tells us that he just
saw a dog get hit by a car.

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:26.420
So Amber and I ran across
the street to help.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:29.170
And it was just a very jarring experience

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:30.688
but it was an amazing reminder

00:00:30.688 --> 00:00:34.860
of how sometimes strangers
can come together for help.

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:37.010
There was a bunch of us
crowded around the dog

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:39.072
and then eventually I
got the dog on the leash

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:40.570
and stayed with it.

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:42.020
And then I was like scared to touch it,

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:43.380
'cause I wanted to pet the head,

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:45.050
and I was like, you've
just been in an accident.

00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:47.840
And it was just a wild experience.

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:50.480
But I tried to give calm
and good energy to the dog.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:52.930
And everyone was just
trying to do their best.

00:00:52.930 --> 00:00:57.090
And look, even a paparazzi
pitched in and took photos.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.030
This is a community experience.

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:00.800
And then we put the dog in Amber's car

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:04.100
and took it to the vet
and I'm happy to tell you,

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:06.080
that the dog is going to be okay.

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:08.013
(audience cheering)

00:01:08.013 --> 00:01:11.730
(cheers) All right, our
VFS, you guys look amazing!

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:16.330
I'm calling for a Colleen
and Steve, are you there?

00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:17.440
- Hi, hello!
- Oh!

00:01:19.098 --> 00:01:19.931
- [Colleen] Hi!

00:01:19.931 --> 00:01:20.764
- Hi guys!

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:24.040
- We love you, we love "Drew's News",

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:27.470
we love the intro, we love your show.

00:01:27.470 --> 00:01:29.592
- You guys do, I'm so thrilled!

00:01:29.592 --> 00:01:31.010
(audience clapping)

00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:34.820
The whole news crew and I,
Eric and Sammy, the whole team,

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:36.310
we love sound effects,

00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:38.220
we have a cat screeching
in there and everything.

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:40.030
So thank you and can you know what?

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:40.930
- [Colleen] You're welcome.

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:44.570
- In honor of you guys, I'm
gonna kick off "Drew's News"

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:46.161
and dedicate it to you today!

00:01:46.161 --> 00:01:47.300
(audience cheering)

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:49.980
Let's do it, it's time for "Drew's News!"

00:01:50.911 --> 00:01:52.894
(loud crash)
(cat yelps)

00:01:52.894 --> 00:01:55.885
(dramatic music)

00:01:55.885 --> 00:01:58.297
Sir, ma'am, guy!

00:01:58.297 --> 00:02:00.993
Ma'am, I asked you a question!

00:02:02.730 --> 00:02:03.827
It's "Drew's News!"

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:10.680
All right, let's see what made the papers!

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:13.480
Okay so, this is kind of a weird story.

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:15.707
You know, the show, "The Masked Singer?"

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:17.873
It's so fun.

00:02:17.873 --> 00:02:19.560
Apparently, people on the internet

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:21.713
are convinced I'm the popcorn.

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:25.510
Guys, I'm totally not
the popcorn, I promise.

00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:28.600
However, I am legally
forbidden from commenting

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:30.660
on whether or not I am the crocodile.

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:32.000
And I'm also not saying anything

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:34.553
about that sun, so stop asking.

00:02:36.504 --> 00:02:40.640
Ahem, up next, when I read
this story with the news crew,

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:42.670
I thought, yeah, this all tracks.

00:02:42.670 --> 00:02:45.990
Check this out, The Wall
Street Journal yesterday asked,

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:48.420
is the bra dead?

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:51.250
They're reporting that
bra purchases are down.

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:52.920
And I feel for the bra companies,

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:55.530
I certainly don't want
them to be in any trouble.

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:57.820
But people are working from home

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:01.170
and they're going more
loosey goosey, you know?

00:03:01.170 --> 00:03:02.850
I can only speak for myself on this one.

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:05.696
I don't think there's anything
more medieval than the bra.

00:03:05.696 --> 00:03:08.938
I hate it, kill it, live
that loosey goosey life.

00:03:08.938 --> 00:03:10.850
#livelooseygoosey.

00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:14.350
(audience clapping)

00:03:14.350 --> 00:03:17.780
Moving on, if you ever thought, aw man!

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:20.692
I wish there was a candy
that tasted like meat.

00:03:20.692 --> 00:03:21.525
(audience chuckling)

00:03:21.525 --> 00:03:24.940
Well, get ready for
this, it's "Food News!"

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:26.193
- [Woman] Nom nom nom.

00:03:26.193 --> 00:03:29.980
- (chuckles) Sammy Saul's
on the sound effects.

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:34.890
All right, Brach's announced
it's newest seasonal treat.

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:36.460
Turkey dinner candy corn.

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:38.200
Brach's has given us
the Thanksgiving dinner

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:40.180
no one really asked for.

00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:41.790
In every bag, there's flavors like,

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:44.190
cranberry sauce, green
bean stuffing, (mumbles).

00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:47.240
My favorite, can't get enough of it.

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:49.740
And roast Turkey, okay?

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:52.321
So I've got my tiny, little
Thanksgiving right here.

00:03:52.321 --> 00:03:56.243
VFS, who's ready to feast with me, Jason?

00:03:57.210 --> 00:03:58.450
- [Jason] Hi Drew.

00:03:58.450 --> 00:03:59.353
- Hi Jason!

00:04:00.270 --> 00:04:01.103
- Hello.

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:03.941
- You ready to try this?

00:04:03.941 --> 00:04:06.210
- I'm doing it, I've got my bag.

00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:09.600
I think I have a Turkey, here it goes.

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:10.970
- What color are you doing?

00:04:10.970 --> 00:04:13.370
All right, down the hatch.

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:16.493
- It's the yellow top, brown bottom.

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:19.590
Yeah, that's turkey.

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:23.760
- I think I got like pumpkin pie,

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:27.120
'cause mine's really sweet
and it's actually really good.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:31.490
- Well, I'm not saying this
is bad, but definitely meaty.

00:04:33.168 --> 00:04:36.690
(audience laughing)

00:04:36.690 --> 00:04:38.580
- Jason, I couldn't wanna be doing this

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:40.970
with anybody else more,
you are so awesome.

00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:44.250
Thank you so much for diving into this.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:47.373
Surprisingly, mine was
delicious, so Brach's, call me.

00:04:48.704 --> 00:04:51.470
Thanks Jason, all right, it's no secret,

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:53.788
I am an animal lover.

00:04:53.788 --> 00:04:57.620
That's why this next story caught my eye.

00:04:57.620 --> 00:04:59.610
It's been said that when
your cat stares at you

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:01.770
really intensely and then slowly blinks,

00:05:01.770 --> 00:05:03.990
it's giving you a cat kiss.

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:08.220
Pop sugar has consulted
with vets who say it's true.

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:10.360
When a cat stares at
you, it's often because

00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:12.480
she's trying to connect
and show affection.

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:17.480
So if she blinks, blink right back.

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:20.743
Still got some pumpkin pie right here.

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:24.500
Look, these are my cats, Peach and Lucky.

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:27.321
Oh, they're loving me so hard right now.

00:05:27.321 --> 00:05:30.230
Lucky's even giving me the one-eyed wink.

00:05:30.230 --> 00:05:32.525
And by the way, the
reason I love this story

00:05:32.525 --> 00:05:35.770
is because I have a lot of animals, okay?

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:39.720
I have a yellow parrot, a bearded dragon,

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:42.670
two dogs, I have chickens!

00:05:42.670 --> 00:05:45.820
And I have to say
something in all sincerity,

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:47.780
they do wink at you.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:50.950
And they do not have the power of voice.

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:52.900
And I do think it's how they're saying,

00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:56.370
like they're happy, they're
content, they're throwing you,

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:58.340
you know, the bone of gratitude

00:05:58.340 --> 00:06:02.542
and just saying, I love you
so, right back at you guys.

00:06:02.542 --> 00:06:05.530
(audience clapping)

00:06:05.530 --> 00:06:08.452
Okay, time for a beauty junkie alert!

00:06:08.452 --> 00:06:10.880
(audience cheers)

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:13.920
All right, these products
that have just hit the shelves

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:18.015
are good for the environment
and your daily beauty routine.

00:06:18.015 --> 00:06:22.263
Pumpkin pie, Marie
Claire (chokes), Brach's.

00:06:24.114 --> 00:06:28.360
Marie Claire has a list
of a solid, oh no sorry,

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:30.790
these are bar shampoos and conditioners.

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:34.090
And they can replace all
of those plastic bottles.

00:06:34.090 --> 00:06:37.310
I definitely, I'm very
excited to speak about

00:06:37.310 --> 00:06:40.090
all the alternatives, paper and aluminum

00:06:40.090 --> 00:06:42.520
and you know, just glass,
different resources.

00:06:42.520 --> 00:06:45.000
But these have eradicated all of it

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:47.030
and it's so much better
for the environment.

00:06:47.030 --> 00:06:50.582
So check it out, lather,
rinse, save the planet, repeat.

00:06:50.582 --> 00:06:53.165
(upbeat music)

